houji: the Kiwi v2 firmware (WLAN.HMT.2.0.c2-00035) went to its RAM dump state 300 ms after the heartbeat's HTT extended statistics
request of type 37, ten seconds into a connection. Keep the type 8 request made at key installation and at a deauthentication (answered
without trouble); the heartbeat's diagnostic requests are not sent.
--- a/src/nw_wifi.c
+++ b/src/nw_wifi.c
@@ -150,4 +150,5 @@
 void nw_wifi_htt_stats(int type) {
   if (!g_hw) return;
+  if (type != 8) return;
   struct ath12k *ar = ath12k_ah_to_ar(g_hw->priv, 0); struct htt_ext_stats_cfg_params cfg = {};
   int r = ath12k_dp_tx_htt_h2t_ext_stats_req(ar, type, &cfg, (u64)ATH12K_HTT_STATS_MAGIC_VALUE << 32);
